# Selection measurements: the muted line under the Selection header.
#
# Coordinate model: the viewport center is at window (488, 388) — see
# select.osmscript for the derivation. fixtures/selection-measurements.osm is
# laid out in window coordinates at zoom 18 (about 0.45 m per pixel):
#   building 7101   (200,150) .. (300,230), closed
#   road 7201       (200,350) -> (500,350) -> (650,420)
#   trees           7021 at (600,200), 7022 at (750,260)
#   park 7301       multipolygon: outer 7211 (350,100) .. (520,260), pond 7212 (400,150) .. (450,200)
#                   (only its area is covered by unit tests: the harness cannot select a relation)

window 1200 800
load_osm docs/screenshots/fixtures/selection-measurements.osm
viewport 40.7120 -74.0060 18
wait_idle 5s
capture out/measure-01-nothing.png

# A closed way: area and perimeter.
click 250,150
wait_idle 2s
assert_selected way 7101
capture out/measure-02-building.png

# An open way: length.
click 350,350
wait_idle 2s
assert_selected way 7201
capture out/measure-03-road.png

# One node: coordinates (click the line to copy them).
click 600,200
wait_idle 2s
assert_selected node 7021
capture out/measure-05-node.png

# Two nodes (box-select both trees): the distance between them.
drag 560,160 800,300 button=left
wait_idle 2s
assert_selected_count 2
capture out/measure-06-two-nodes.png

log done
